<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Austro-Russian–Turkish War (1735–1739)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1735–1739</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Austro-Russian–Turkish War of 1735–1739 was fought between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, joined in 1737 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>. The Russians took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azov">Azov</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ochakiv">Ochakov</a> and won at Stavuchany, but Austria was defeated at Grocka in 1739 and by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-belgrade">Treaty of Belgrade</a> returned northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a>, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgrade">Belgrade</a>, to the Ottomans, while Russia kept only Azov, without the right to fortify it.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/austro-russian-turkish-war-1735-1739.jpg" alt="Austro-Russian–Turkish War (1735–1739)" width="320" height="165" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anik Benoit · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Siege_of_Ochakov_(1737).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
